  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n\nThe optimization challenge arises from the non-convex nature of the overlap integral, causing local minima that trap gradient-based methods like SLSQP. To address this, we employ a multi-start strategy with perturbed initial guesses, enhancing the likelihood of discovering a global minimum. Each perturbation maintains the integral constraint, ensuring feasible search points.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n\nWe represent h as a step function with n_points samples over [0,2], where each h[i] \u2208 [0,1] and \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x) dx = 1. The objective is min\u2095 max\u2096 \u222b h(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx, discretized as max(np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\")) * dx. The constraints are:\n\n- 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n- sum(h) = n_points / 2\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n\na. Validate and store initial_h_values.\nb. Generate M initial guesses:\n   - Start with initial_h_values.\n   - For each additional guess, randomly perturb 10% of the values, ensuring the sum constraint by redistributing excess or deficit.\nc. For each guess:\n   i. Use SLSQP to minimize the overlap integral.\n   ii. Track the best solution (lowest C5) found.\n   iii. If the budget permits, restart with a new initial guess.\nd. After exhausting the budget, return the best feasible solution.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n\n- Start with M=10 initial guesses.\n- Perturb each guess by adjusting up to 10% of the h[i] values, preserving the sum.\n- Use a perturbation radius of 0.1 (clamped to [0,1]).\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n\nEach SLSQP run with n_points=95 takes \u2248100s. With M=10, we allocate 1000s, leaving 100s for perturbations and final checks. If runs exceed budget, stop and return the best candidate.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n\nEach candidate is validated for feasibility:\n- Check 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1.\n- Verify sum(h) = n_points / 2 within 1e-6 tolerance.\n\nThe final h, c5_value, and n_points are returned, with c5_value computed from the evaluator to ensure accuracy.",
